cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Cite this software and reproduction release. The software DOI was reserved
  at archive assembly; publication is handled separately.
type: software
title: 'Conditional flow matching in acute human wounds: analysis software and reproduction
  archive'
authors:
- family-names: Fu
  given-names: Zeyu
version: 0.5.0
license: MIT
abstract: A three-donor audit of population reconstruction by conditional flow matching
  in acute human wounds. The release includes the producing programs, public processed
  counts, frozen coordinates, saved fields and predictions, numerical evidence, protocols
  and corrected journal documents. It distinguishes global time holdout from donor
  transfer, retains adverse control comparisons and records strict replay limits.
  The analysis does not identify individual cell trajectories or validate clinical
  wound prognosis.
repository-code: https://github.com/PeterPonyu/wound-population-dynamics
keywords:
- single-cell transcriptomics
- wound healing
- population dynamics
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23308074
